<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Activity</title>
<para>Solve each equation by rewriting it in factored form and using the zero product property. Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+ 12x + 11 = 0\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-1\) and \(x=-11\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2− 3 = 1\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-2\) and \(x=2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2− 6x + 7 = -2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=3\)</para>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>Press Pause</title>
<para>If students are still making substantial errors with factoring, spend some time reviewing student work from cool downs and providing additional practice opportunities through practice problems.</para></section>
</content>
